From 11125e4d168c8e872588dc36937de2b146bd43f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Corios00 <52224974+Corios00@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:57:27 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] The cameraman cuts away from a wall filling the picture,
 never films from the void, and frames a duel closer

A cabin's corner filled a third to half of VanCleef's takes for a minute at a time: the camera cut
only when the boss or hero was hidden, and 0089's eight foreground lines, short of the frame's
edges and counting the floor, scored it low. Now twenty lines out to the edges, the floor not
counted, and the world on seven of them (a third of the picture) for a second is a cut, once the
position has been held 3 s, to one clearly better; they weigh more when a position is chosen.

Round a bend in Rhahk'Zor's tunnel the middle of the two was in the void outside the mine, and the
camera, measured out from there, stood in the void (take 418). The point it looks at is now one the
hero sees, and every position must see the hero or the subject from inside the world.

A duel stands 8 to 12 yd out (was 10 to 14, the two small in the picture), and the fight's axis
turns over 1.5 s (was 0.8), so the camera doesn't swing round into walls as the two circle.
